From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: ingenic: register the T31 GPIO banks

The T31 pinctrl chip registers, but its GPIO child nodes use compatible
"ingenic,t31-gpio", which is missing from ingenic_gpio_of_matches.
ingenic_gpio_probe() therefore never runs for them, no gpiochip is
created, and every gpiod consumer on the SoC defers forever (gpio-leds,
gpio-keys, and any driver that requests a pin - e.g. the SDIO reset).
The sysfs GPIO ABI is dead as well. Add the t31-gpio compatible so the
banks are registered.

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
@@ -4528,6 +4528,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,jz4770-gpio" },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,jz4775-gpio" },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,jz4780-gpio" },
+	{ .compatible = "ingenic,t31-gpio" },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,x1000-gpio" },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,x1600-gpio" },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,x1830-gpio" },
